    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Graphs are versatile and powerful data structures used to model various relationships and connections. Understanding the different types of graphs—such as directed, undirected, weighted, and unweighted—along with their representations (adjacency matrix and adjacency list), is crucial for solving problems in computer science and real-world applications. Graph traversal techniques like BFS and DFS are foundational for operations like pathfinding, cycle detection, and connectivity analysis."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Whether dealing with simple networks, complex routing algorithms, or hierarchical structures, graphs provide a flexible framework for solving a wide range of computational problems efficiently."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 88,
      "subsections": []
    }
